<section id="currency" class="scroll-mt-20 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
      <div class="w-full order-last lg:order-none">
        <img src="/images/feature-currency-tracking.png" alt="NinerLog currency tracking dashboard with EASA revalidation and FAA 90-day currency status" class="rounded-xl shadow-xl w-full dark:hidden" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" />
        <img src="/images/feature-currency-tracking-dark.png" alt="NinerLog currency tracking dashboard with EASA revalidation and FAA 90-day currency status" class="rounded-xl shadow-xl w-full hidden dark:block" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" />
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-4">Never guess whether you are current</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          NinerLog evaluates your flights against the rules of whichever authority issued the licence, and tells you the date your currency runs out rather than making you count backwards from today.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          {{ check("EASA revalidation by experience (FCL.740) and passenger currency") }}
          {{ check("FAA 90-day passenger currency (14 CFR 61.57), night currency, and the flight review (61.56)") }}
          {{ check("Instrument currency with approach and hold counting, and IPC tracking") }}
          {{ check("<strong>90-day recency, per model and per registration.</strong> Three takeoffs and landings in the last 90 days, tracked by type the way FCL.060(b) defines it &mdash; and optionally per tail number as a familiarity aid", true) }}
          {{ check("<strong>Told before it bites.</strong> An expiry banner on the dashboard with the next step spelled out, and email reminders at 30, 14 and 7 days &mdash; or whichever days you choose", true) }}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 3b — Custom currency rules. The headline addition; shown as the rule itself. -->
<section class="bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
      <div class="reveal">
        {{ badge("WRITE YOUR OWN") }}
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-4 mt-3">Currency rules nobody else ships</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Your club wants five landings a quarter. Your insurer wants ten hours on type a year. Your own personal minimum is a night landing every other month. None of that is in any regulation, so no logbook has a card for it &mdash; until you build one.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          A rule is three things: how far back to look, which flights count, and what you need. Drag it together in the block editor or write the YAML directly &mdash; the two are the same rule, and you can switch between them mid-edit.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          {{ check("<strong>Twenty-five metrics.</strong> Flights, landings and takeoffs (day or night), approaches, holds, and time as PIC, dual, night, IFR or cross-country") }}
          {{ check("<strong>Filter down to what counts.</strong> By aircraft class, type or registration, by complex, high-performance or tailwheel, by PIC or dual, night, IFR or cross-country") }}
          {{ check("<strong>Preview against your real logbook.</strong> See whether the rule you just wrote says you are current &mdash; before you save it") }}
          {{ check("<strong>A card like any other.</strong> Sits on your currency page with its own emoji and its own &ldquo;current until&rdquo; date; pause it and it fades and sinks rather than disappearing") }}
          {{ check("<strong>Reminders per rule.</strong> Ring the bell on the ones worth an email; leave the rest quiet") }}
          {{ check("<strong>Share it with a link.</strong> Publish a rule, send the link to your club, and every member imports it in one click. Turn sharing off and the link dies") }}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal reveal-delay-1 lg:sticky lg:top-24">
        <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 shadow-xl">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2.5 bg-slate-100 dark:bg-navy-800 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-rose-400/70" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-amber-400/70" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400/70" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="ml-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">night-landings.yaml</span>
          </div>
<pre class="bg-navy-950 text-slate-300 p-5 overflow-x-auto text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed font-mono"><code><span class="text-slate-400"># Give your rule a name and an emoji.</span>
<span class="text-sky-400">name</span>: Night landings
<span class="text-sky-400">emoji</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"&#x1F319;"</span>
<span class="text-sky-400">description</span>: Stay night-current for passengers.

<span class="text-slate-400"># How far back to look.</span>
<span class="text-sky-400">window</span>:
  <span class="text-sky-400">amount</span>: <span class="text-emerald-400">90</span>
  <span class="text-sky-400">unit</span>: days

<span class="text-slate-400"># Which flights count.</span>
<span class="text-sky-400">filters</span>:
  - <span class="text-sky-400">field</span>: has_night
    <span class="text-sky-400">op</span>: is_true

<span class="text-slate-400"># What you need to stay current.</span>
<span class="text-sky-400">requirements</span>:
  - <span class="text-sky-400">metric</span>: night_landings
    <span class="text-sky-400">min</span>: <span class="text-emerald-400">3</span>
    <span class="text-sky-400">label</span>: Night landings
</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl">
          <img src="/images/feature-custom-currency.png" alt="The NinerLog custom currency builder editing the night-landings rule, with its timeframe, filter and requirement blocks" class="w-full dark:hidden" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" />
          <img src="/images/feature-custom-currency-dark.png" alt="The NinerLog custom currency builder editing the night-landings rule, with its timeframe, filter and requirement blocks" class="w-full hidden dark:block" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" />
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
          The same rule in the block editor: a 90-day window, one filter, one requirement. Nothing to install, nothing to script.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
